.TH "SKOGAI MEMORY-INDEX" 1  "skogai memory-index 0.0.0" 
.SH NAME
skogai memory\-index \- index lines for entries missing from the index, and index links to missing files. pure unless \-\-apply
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBskogai memory index\fR [OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.br
index lines for entries missing from the index, and index links to missing files. pure unless \-\-apply
.br

.br
exit 1 when something is out of sync and \-\-apply was not given.
.br
\-\-apply appends the missing lines; dead links are only reported.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-apply\fR
.br
append the missing lines to the index
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
.br
Print help
